 4. 🍏 5,486 days of Cook 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Apple CEO Tim Cook. Photo: Justin Sullivan/Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Tim Cook isn't exactly pulling the plug on his Apple tenure — but today is his last day as CEO after 15 years on the job.

 Cook recently announced plans to step down as CEO and become executive chair — with senior VP of hardware engineering John Ternus taking the top job beginning Tuesday. State of play: During Cook's tenure, Apple shareholders enjoyed gains of more than 2,500%, multiple stock splits and a long stretch as the world's most valuable company, according to Freedom Capital Markets.

 The tech giant added the Apple Watch, AirPods and TV products during his reign, while it dramatically expanded its services arm. Yes, but: Cook leaves amid questions over whether Apple is falling behind in the AI race.

 
 
