 🗓️ On this day in 1602, the Dutch East India Company closed the world's first public IPO. The offering drew 1,143 investors, one of the last of whom was a maid of Dirck van Os, the company co-founder whose house served as the official bookkeeping office. For a month, Neeltgen Cornelis watched people pour in to get in on the deal, triggering perhaps the earliest recorded case of retail investor FOMO.

